=== Lurandia ===

Petran Catholicism is the dominant religion of [[Guajicutea]] (66 per cent of the population) and of [[Potocsí]] (71.2 per cent), and the largest single denomination of [[Balboa]] (approximately 40 per cent), practised principally by the white, mixed, and rural Black populations and organised under the [[Archdiocese of Sant Bart]]. In [[Balisca]], Catholics constitute 10 per cent of the population, a share reduced by the strong anti-clericalism of the revolutionary period and the country's exceptional level of irreligion. A Burawi Catholic minority of approximately 4 per cent exists in Guajicutea, concentrated around Waribá.

